T7suite-iOS
Native Swift port workbench, 2026.

Based in part on the formats and algorithms in TuningSuites / T7Suite,
by the TuningSuites contributors, including Dilemma and Mattias Claesson.
Original project: https://github.com/mattiasclaesson/TuningSuites
User-provided source archive: TuningSuites-T7suite_v0.1.59.0.tar.gz
Archive SHA-256: 78c688d0703ec20dc30e46253e117943c28d1beedbd3707dcc7c2a03c5e74978
The original archive's Apache License 2.0 is retained in LICENSE.

The Swift symbol decompressor and packed/unpacked symbol readers are rewrites
of the corresponding CommonSuite and T7Suite algorithms. Changes include
instance-local decoder state, bounded parsing, explicit malformed-input errors,
Huffman rescaling correction, and removal of guessed address repair.
The legacy Saab KWP frame format and T7 footer layout were studied from the
source archive. The UI, edit model, document handling, tests and Swift types are
new implementations. Source comments identify relevant references.

The separate mattiasclaesson/Trionic project was consulted as a format and
checksum reference. No TrionicCANLib DLL or verbatim source file from that
repository is redistributed here. Further imports require license review.

Original ECU firmware, Windows installers, manuals, vendor DLLs, DevExpress,
Nevron, Office components and adapter libraries are not included. Their rights
are not granted by this repository's license. The new bit reader does not copy
the separately licensed CommonSuite/BitStream.cs implementation.

